  "live_records": {
    "q-101209": {
      "dom_id": "step-q101209",
      "name": "Question 1",
      "problem": "Find the value of $\\frac{2}{9}-\\frac{7}{9}.$",
      "worked_solution": "Since both fractions have the same denominators, we can combine them into one fraction, which gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{2}{9}-\\frac{7}{9}=\\frac{2-7}{9}.\n$$\n\nNow, we work out $2-7$ using a number line:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14148354/assets/bb81cb03e8205a9df3a62ed47ca7b2a4c1a66ad990eaf248f8701480bb2d5bb1.png)\n\nSo, we get \n\n$$\n\\frac{2-7}{9}=\\frac{-5}{9}=-\\frac{5}{9}.\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
