    "q-119461": {
      "dom_id": "step-q119461",
      "name": "Question 4",
      "problem": "Find the value of $\\frac{2}{7}-\\frac{6}{7}.$",
      "worked_solution": "Since both fractions have the same denominators, we can combine them into one fraction, which gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{2}{7}-\\frac{6}{7}=\\frac{2-6}{7}.\n$$\n\nNow, we work out $2-6$ using a number line:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14148354/assets/6709a58db6cc2c9d5b5811282fcf34d5d6766b7dba9f9f46db5cabacbd90f95d.png)\n\nSo, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{2-6}{7}=\\frac{-4}{7}=-\\frac{4}{7}.\n$$",
