    "q-119466": {
      "dom_id": "step-q119466",
      "name": "Question 5",
      "problem": "Find the value of $-\\frac{3}{11}-\\frac{6}{11}.$",
      "worked_solution": "Since both fractions have the same denominators, we can combine them into one fraction, which gives\n\n$$\n-\\frac{3}{11}-\\frac{6}{11}=\\frac{-3-6}{11}.\n$$\n\nNow, we work out $-3-6$ using a number line:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14148354/assets/24970f00ebf3ea583b8cd56831990f5d501ecaf1c87091e194c02ee7ecc0ff70.png)\n\nSo, we get \n\n$$\n\\frac{-3-6}{11}=\\frac{-9}{11}=-\\frac{9}{11}.\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
