    "q-101213": {
      "dom_id": "step-q101213",
      "name": "Question 9",
      "problem": "Calculate the value of $\\frac{2}{3}-\\frac{5}{6}.$",
      "worked_solution": "We write $\\frac{2}{3}$ as $\\frac{4}{6}$ and then we simply subtract the numerators. This gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{4}{6}-\\frac{5}{6}=\\frac{4-5}{6}.\n$$\n\nNow, we work out $4-5$ using a number line:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14148354/assets/53b1655255807f7007040bb6ba38c2570ec14e0dde04e3d49696953f3750d449.png)\n\nSo we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{4-5}{6}=\\frac{-1}{6}=-\\frac{1}{6}.\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
