    "q-119510": {
      "dom_id": "step-q119510",
      "name": "Question 11",
      "problem": "Calculate the value of $\\frac{4}{9}-\\frac{1}{2}.$",
      "worked_solution": "We write $\\frac{4}{9}$ as $\\frac{8}{18}$ and $\\frac{1}{2}$ as $\\frac{9}{18},$ and then we simply subtract the numerators. This gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{8}{18}-\\frac{9}{18}=\\frac{8-9}{18}.\n$$\n\nNow, we work out $8-9$ using a number line:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14148354/assets/617ce139a9838991ce1fe0532a01da77e3e58f9e5d50184598570419b4c5a5fc.png)\n\nSo, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{8-9}{18}=\\frac{-1}{18}=-\\frac{1}{18}.\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
