    "q-119508": {
      "dom_id": "step-q119508",
      "name": "Question 12",
      "problem": "Calculate the value of $\\frac{2}{7}-\\frac{1}{3}.$",
      "worked_solution": "We write $\\frac{2}{7}$ as $\\frac{6}{21}$ and $\\frac{1}{3}$ as $\\frac{7}{21},$ and then we simply subtract the numerators. This gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{6}{21}-\\frac{7}{21}=\\frac{6-7}{21}.\n$$\n\nNow, we work out $6-7$ using a number line:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14148354/assets/f39be0767b6d9b5c3203946adc4212201c49cd6539cfc49c3c75646d7ea4bac5.png)\n\nSo, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{6-7}{21}=\\frac{-1}{21}=-\\frac{1}{21}.\n$$",
