    "q-119393": {
      "dom_id": "step-q119393",
      "name": "Question 18",
      "problem": "Find the value of $\\frac{2}{5}-1\\,\\frac{1}{5}.$",
      "worked_solution": "First, we write $1\\,\\frac{1}{5}$ as an improper fraction:\n\n$$\n1\\,\\frac{1}{5}=\\frac{(1\\times 5)+1}{5}=\\frac{6}{5}\n$$\n\nSince both fractions have the same denominators, we can combine them into one fraction, which gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{2}{5}-\\frac{6}{5}=\\frac{2-6}{5}.\n$$\n\nNow, we work out $2-6$ using a number line:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14148354/assets/ed6c51ffa37fa80ca17575c241738c602cb81cb2bca500fea1fb3231063763b2.png)\n\nSo, we get \n\n$$\n\\frac{2-6}{5}=\\frac{-4}{5}=-\\frac{4}{5}.\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices": [
            {
              "option": "a",
              "dom_id": "questionWidget-choiceLetterCircle-119393-a",
              "type": "math",
              "value": "\\frac{1}{5}",
              "html": "<mjx-container class=\"MathJax CtxtMenu_Attached_0\" jax=\"CHTML\" tabindex=\"0\" ctxtmenu_counter=\"202\" style=\"font-size: 119.6%; position: relative;\"><mjx-math class=\"MJX-TEX\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><mjx-mstyle><mjx-mfrac><mjx-frac type=\"d\"><mjx-num><mjx-nstrut type=\"d\"></mjx-nstrut><mjx-mn class=\"mjx-n\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c31\"></mjx-c></mjx-mn></mjx-num><mjx-dbox><mjx-dtable><mjx-line type=\"d\"></mjx-line><mjx-row><mjx-den><mjx-dstrut type=\"d\"></mjx-dstrut><mjx-mn class=\"mjx-n\"><mjx-c class=\"mjx-c35\"></mjx-c></mjx-mn></mjx-den></mjx-row></mjx-dtable></mjx-dbox></mjx-frac></mjx-mfrac></mjx-mstyle></mjx-math><mjx-assistive-mml unselectable=\"on\" display=\"inline\"><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mstyle displaystyle=\"true\" scriptlevel=\"0\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>5</mn></mfrac></mstyle></math></mjx-assistive-mml></mjx-container>"
            },
            {
